===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leh₂is-|*leh₃is-}}
The {{lg|adjective}}, {{lg|determiner}}, and {{lg|noun}} are derived from {{inh|en|enm|leste}}, {{m|enm|lest}}, {{m|enm|last|t=(''adjective'') smallest, least; (''noun'') smallest thing, etc.; person or thing least in importance; etc.}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=lē̆st(e|pos=''adj.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED25244}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|lǣst}},<ref>{{R:Anglo-Saxon Dictionary|entry=læst: ''see'' læssa|pos=''adj. cpve.'' {{quote-gloss|comparative}}|noformat=1|page=612|column=1}}</ref> a contraction of {{m|ang|læsast}}, {{m|ang|læsest|t=least}} (also {{m|ang|lærest}} in only one source),<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'', ''pron.'', ''n.'', and ''adv|id=9824936291|date=December 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=det.'', ''pron.'', ''adv.'', and ''adj|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220117021252/https://www.lexico.com/definition/least}}</ref> from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*laisistaz|t=smallest, least}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*laisiz|t=less}} (possibly from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*leh₂is-}} or {{m|ine-pro|*leh₃is-}}; whence modern {{cog|en|less}}) + {{m|gem-pro|*-istaz|t={{lg|suffix}} forming {{lg|superlative}} forms of some adjectives}}.

The {{lg|adverb}} and {{lg|pronoun}} are derived from the adjective or determiner.

